n a new giant factory at Castle Bromwich in Southampton where a total of 920 Mk IIs were built. The Mk II came into service in time for the Battle of Britain in 1940, but the Mk I and Mk II were more or less phased out in 1941 and replaced with the Mk V.","LocalizedString":"The Supermarine Spitfire was a British fighter aircraft that was first introduced in 1938 and was used by the Royal Air Force and the Allied air forces during WWII. The Mk II varied from the Mk I as it used the Merlin XIII engine, which gave it an increase of 120 horsepower over the engines used in the Mk I. Another main difference was that it was produced in a new giant factory at Castle Bromwich in Southampton where a total of 920 Mk IIs were built. The Mk II came into service in time for the Battle of Britain in 1940, but the Mk I and Mk II were more or less phased out in 1941 and replaced with the Mk V."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","isReserved":true,"showBoostIcon":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardLocationMoved","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardAblitiesChanged"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Guarded"],"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Card_Blowups/AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Breakthrough/t_spitfire_mk_ii.t_spitfire_mk_ii","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Jarosław Wróbel","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/SPITFIRE_Mk_II.SPITFIRE_Mk_II","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":314.0},"historyPhotoSource":"Imperial War Museum","historyPhotoIdentificationCode":"CH 5291","historyPhotoAuthor":"Royal Air Force official photographer","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_spitfire_mk_ii_photo","SourceString":"Spitfire Mk  IIA of the Air 